From d054faf0712ea2dfeb26952839d3751230cbb26a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Bharat Dintakurti <bdintakurti@nvidia.com>
Date: Wed, 12 Aug 2026 09:31:24 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 3/6] NVIDIA: SAUCE: usb: xhci-mtk-v2: add ACPI power
 management support

BugLink: https://bugs.launchpad.net/bugs/2167884

Add the MediaTek xHCI platform glue for ACPI-described controllers.
Parse the IPPC, MAC and PHY resources, configure the USB PHYs, and
coordinate controller D0/D3 transitions through Power Wrap. Add support
for the platform's dedicated wake interrupt.

Integrate the platform sequence with probe, remove and system suspend.
Propagate IPPC and Power Wrap failures, unwind locally prepared hardware
on probe and suspend failures, and avoid MMIO recovery until firmware has
confirmed D0. Follow the platform power-on ordering by disabling IPPC bus
and PHY clock gating before releasing host power-down during initialization
and low-power exit.

Keep runtime PM disabled until Power Wrap can report an authoritative
state after a failed transition, and reject MediaTek runtime PM callbacks.
Keep confirmed D0 after system-resume errors. If platform D0 exit fails,
mark both HCDs inaccessible; if controller restore or failed-suspend
rollback fails after D0, keep accessibility accurate while marking the host
dead before later IRQ, hub, unlink, remove, or shutdown paths can access
registers.

Quiesce Debug Capability work and tear down its software state without
MMIO when hardware is inaccessible. Suppress stale clear-TT doorbells
during failed-host teardown.

Validate the required PHY type before acquiring controller resources,
return standard timeout errors, and avoid hardware teardown when D0 is not
confirmed.

Co-developed-by: Chunfeng Yun <chunfeng.yun@mediatek.com>
Signed-off-by: Chunfeng Yun <chunfeng.yun@mediatek.com>
